  "text": "The `pricing.ts` file defines a function `priceFor` that calculates the price of an item based on its stock level [S1]. It sets a base price of 250 cents and applies a doubling surcharge when stock is low [S1]. This function relies on the `stockLevel` function from `inventory.ts` to determine if an item's stock is low [S1].  \n\n`inventory.ts` imports `priceFor` and defines the `Item` interface and `stockLevel` function, which is used by `pricing.ts` to evaluate stock conditions [S2][S3]. Thus, `pricing.ts` depends on `inventory.ts` for stock-level data to adjust prices [S1][S3].  \n\nThe relationship is that `pricing.ts` uses data from `inventory.ts` to dynamically adjust prices based on stock levels.",
